@page "/privacy"
@inject AccountState AccountState

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - Sprite Scout</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <PageMetadata Title="Privacy Policy - Sprite Scout"
                  Description="Learn how Sprite Scout handles account details, collection progress, cookies, local storage, and public Fortnite Sprite profiles."
                  Path="/privacy">
        <OpenGraphMetadata />
        <TwitterCardMetadata />
    </PageMetadata>
</HeadContent>

<main>
    <SiteHeader Profile="@AccountState.Profile" IsAccountLoading="@(!AccountState.IsLoaded)" />

    <section class="legalPage">
        <header class="legalHero">
            <span class="sectionKicker">LEGAL & DATA PROTECTION</span>
            <h1>PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
            <p class="lastUpdated">Last updated: August 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="legalContent">
            <div class="highlightBox">
                <h3>Our Privacy Promise in Brief</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Minimal Data Collection:</strong> We do not store your email address, Google profile photo, or real name.</li>
                    <li><strong>No Trackers or Ads:</strong> We do not use third-party analytics trackers, advertising networks, or data brokers.</li>
                    <li><strong>Local by Default:</strong> Guest checklist progress is stored exclusively in your browser.</li>
                    <li><strong>Immediate Account Deletion:</strong> You can permanently wipe your account and all associated progress at any time from your Account settings.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <section>
                <h2>1. About Sprite Scout</h2>
                <p>
                    Sprite Scout ("we", "us", or "our") is an independent, fan-made web companion for tracking Fortnite Sprite collections.
                    This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your personal data when you visit our website, track Sprites locally, or create an account via Google Sign-In.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
                
                <h3>A. Guest Users (No Sign-In)</h3>
                <p>
                    When using Sprite Scout without signing in, your Sprite ownership and mastery checklist progress is saved solely in your web browser's <code>localStorage</code>.
                    This data is not transmitted to our servers or stored in our database.
                </p>

                <h3>B. Signed-In Users (Google Authentication)</h3>
                <p>
                    If you choose to sign in to synchronize your collection across devices or share your progress, we collect only the minimal data necessary to maintain your account:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Google Subject Identifier (<code>sub</code>):</strong> A pseudonymous unique identifier provided by Google OAuth to securely associate your sign-in with your account.</li>
                    <li><strong>Display Name:</strong> A chosen public scout name (defaults to your Google display name, but fully editable by you).</li>
                    <li><strong>Epic Games Display Name (Optional):</strong> If provided by you, used to enable other players to find and compare collections.</li>
                    <li><strong>Sprite Collection Progress:</strong> The IDs of Sprites you have marked as Owned or Mastered.</li>
                    <li><strong>Profile Preferences:</strong> Whether your collection is public or private.</li>
                    <li><strong>Account Timestamps:</strong> Account creation and last-updated timestamps for database integrity.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="noticeText">
                    <strong>What we do NOT collect or store:</strong> We do not store your Google email address, Google avatar/profile picture, Google contacts, or passwords.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>3. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
                <p>Sprite Scout uses only essential technical storage mechanisms:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong><code>sprite-scout-auth</code> Cookie:</strong> An encrypted, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax session cookie used solely to authenticate your requests when you sign in. It expires after 30 days of inactivity.</li>
                    <li><strong>Browser <code>localStorage</code>:</strong> Used to preserve your offline checklist progress, theme preferences, and filter states on your device.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>We do not use tracking cookies, advertising cookies, or third-party behavioral profiling scripts.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>4. How We Use Your Data</h2>
                <p>We process your data strictly to provide the core functionality of Sprite Scout:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>To authenticate your session and maintain your account.</li>
                    <li>To save and synchronize your Sprite collection across devices.</li>
                    <li>To display your public profile and collection comparisons if you enable public sharing.</li>
                    <li>To maintain service reliability, security, and prevent abusive requests.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>5. Third-Party Infrastructure & Processors</h2>
                <p>We use reputable cloud infrastructure to host and operate the application:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Google OAuth:</strong> For secure federated authentication. When you sign in, Google's Privacy Policy applies to the authentication interaction.</li>
                    <li><strong>Microsoft Azure:</strong> Hosts the web application server and container runtime.</li>
                    <li><strong>Supabase / PostgreSQL:</strong> Provides managed database hosting where authenticated account records and progress are stored.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>We do not sell, rent, trade, or monetize your personal information to any third parties.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>6. Data Retention and Account Deletion</h2>
                <p>
                    Your data is retained for as long as your account remains active.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Immediate Account Deletion:</strong> You have complete control over your data. You can permanently delete your profile, Epic display name, and all associated Sprite collection progress at any time by visiting <a href="/account">Account Settings</a> and confirming deletion under the <strong>Danger Zone</strong>. Account deletion is instantaneous and irrevocable.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>7. Your Privacy Rights (GDPR & CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
                <p>
                    Depending on your location, you may have the following rights regarding your personal data:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Right to Access:</strong> You can view all information associated with your account in your Account dashboard or export your checklist as a PDF.</li>
                    <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> You can edit your Display Name and Epic Display Name at any time.</li>
                    <li><strong>Right to Erasure:</strong> You can self-delete your account and all stored records at any time.</li>
                    <li><strong>Right to Restriction / Privacy:</strong> You can toggle your collection between Public and Private at will.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>8. Security</h2>
                <p>
                    We protect your data using industry-standard security measures, including HTTPS/TLS encryption in transit, ASP.NET Core Data Protection encryption for authentication keys, and restricted database connection pooling.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>9. Changes to this Policy</h2>
                <p>
                    We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect enhancements to our service or legal requirements. Updates will be posted on this page with a revised "Last updated" date.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>10. Contact</h2>
                <p>
                    If you have any questions, feedback, or data privacy requests regarding Sprite Scout, please open a <a href="https://github.com/joshua-montgomery-1/fortnite-sprite-tracker/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub issue</a> or contact the project maintainer.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>

    <SiteFooter />
</main>
